Let tsr.config.json configure the TanStack Start route generator.

`getConfig` merges as `{ ...tsr.config.json, ...inlineConfig }`, so every key
oj passes inline silently overrides the app's own configuration. oj passes
`routesDirectory`, `generatedRouteTree`, `autoCodeSplitting` and
`routeFileIgnorePattern` -- all of them documented `tsr.config.json` settings,
and all of them things `@tanstack/router-generator` exists to let an app
choose.

The visible symptom is an app whose route tree is not at the default path. oj
regenerates it at `src/routeTree.gen.ts` regardless, so the app keeps importing
the tree it configured, oj keeps writing one nothing reads, and the source tree
grows a second route tree that is never right. `routeTreeFileFooter` is in the
same schema, so an app that needs a footer (TanStack Start's own `declare
module` block, which the framework's Vite plugin appends) cannot get one either.

Only `target` is genuinely oj's to decide here. The rest become defaults
supplied when the app has not set them, which leaves an app with no
tsr.config.json behaving exactly as before.

Carried here so //oj:dev_server can serve an app whose layout is not the
framework default. Filed upstream as https://github.com/raphamorim/oj/pull/116.

diff --git a/src/assets/start/generate.mjs b/src/assets/start/generate.mjs
--- a/src/assets/start/generate.mjs
+++ b/src/assets/start/generate.mjs
@@ -1,5 +1,8 @@
